# tools/layout/lab-pads.env -- the layout pads of a lab build (tools/build.sh lab).
#
# A lab build carries lab-only code in main() before the frame loop and around
# pace_frame, so the release pads (psp/Makefile) put its loop window 160 B off
# a lab build of round 3 (0802244e).  These values were tuned in claude/opt-1000
# round 7 against that ELF and are what hardware arm C (builds/r7-lab, EBOOT
# 5a3c4b45) was built with.  tools/build.sh lab applies them unless LAB_PADS=0;
# an explicit LAYOUT_PAD_BYTES= or PSP_EXTRA= still overrides them for a sweep.
# Re-tune with tools/layout/layout_lock.py solve lab, then check, then re-record
# [lab] in tools/layout/layout.lock.
# beta.5 base (claude/beta5-base): re-tuned against the round-8 lab ELF 51d607c5
# for the merged beta.4.1 + opt-1000 code; LAYOUT_PAD_MAIN_BYTES is new
# (psp/layout_pad_main.S).  docs/LAYOUT-PINNING.md has the reasoning.
# claude/beta5-hop: re-tuned for HALT_HOP (hot_order.txt late section); same doc.
# beta.5 integration (b5-online, GBC palettes, the filters cache fix): re-tuned;
# LAYOUT_PAD_LATE_BYTES is new (psp/layout_pad_late.S); same doc.
# beta.5 JIT fix (claude/jit-thrash-fix): BSCAN 7800 -> 5496 for hot_order.txt's
# bscan rows (2,304 B in front of B's update_scanline zeros); the rest unchanged.
# HW-1 (claude/hw1-sleep): main's blocks re-ordered around the sleep fixes; MAIN
# 176 -> 8076 puts main at mod 0x0aac (41.3 % of loop-line bytes on the base's
# sets, the best shift; 3.7 % unshifted), TEXT 7792, FE 2528, CORE 7628 and RO 128
# put pace_frame, fe_host_reset, A's cold text and tables back.  Lab boot heap
# -16 KiB (two pages: the 8 KiB-wrapped MAIN shift).  docs/LAYOUT-PINNING.md.
# HW-1 review r2 (claude/hw1-sleep-r2): power_cb grew 8 B (the failed sync no
# longer stops the module; the standby>=2 rung's labels): TEXT 7792 -> 7784,
# CORE 7628 -> 7636; main unmoved.
# HW-1 review r2 follow-ups (the bring-ups' one hold, boot_stop_notice, the
# online cancel's redraw, the wake's ME notice, the harness's ME-quiet log and
# me_fake -1/-2): +516 B before pace_frame, +120 B in me_host.o, four .rodata
# steps.  TEXT 7784 -> 7268, FE 2528 -> 2408; RO 128 -> 8064 (two steps more
# than the pad held, so it wraps: lab boot heap -8 KiB); main unmoved.
# HW-1 H1, the ME-lost notice with no power hold: -76 B before pace_frame.
# TEXT 7268 -> 7344; every other pad and main unmoved.
# HW-1 H1 r5, the ME-lost wake held into the teardown: main +44 B (its address
# unmoved), +96 B more before pace_frame, one .rodata step.  TEXT 7344 -> 7204,
# CORE 7636 -> 7616, RO 8064 -> 8000 (still wrapped: boot heap unchanged).
# HW-2 (claude/hw2-exit): MAIN 176 -> 368 (the loop's best placement), TEXT
# 692 -> 6964, FE 2600 -> 2296, CORE 7708 -> 7692, RO 384 -> 128; then the
# F4 hold (ui_net_action +20 B): TEXT 6964 -> 6944, CORE 7692 -> 7680.
# "As displayed" screenshots: text 692 -> 24, FE 2600 -> 52, GB 956 -> 828,
# CORE 7708 -> 7680, RO 384 -> 8 (docs/LAYOUT-PINNING.md, "Keeping the pads").
LAYOUT_PAD_BYTES=7204
LAYOUT_PAD_BSCAN_BYTES=5496
LAYOUT_PAD_MAIN_BYTES=8076
LAYOUT_PAD_LATE_BYTES=2272
LAYOUT_PAD_FE_BYTES=2408
# LAYOUT_PAD_GB_BYTES: merged opt-1000 round 9-10 (the GB cores' -1040 B).
LAYOUT_PAD_GB_BYTES=956
# 5.0.0 integration: instance A's cold core text back where the beta.4 lab
# layout had it (pipe_latch 0x0460 -> 0x1960: CORE 7708 -> 4892); the RO pad
# takes the 2,816 B back (384 -> 3200), so .rodata, .data and .bss do not move.
LAYOUT_PAD_CORE_BYTES=4800
LAYOUT_PAD_RO_BYTES=2624
# PCARG_SIDE (claude/pcarg-side): the zeros in front of A's translate_block_arm
# (psp/layout_pad_warm.S); the lab translator is 64 B smaller than the release's.
# 5888 -> 5504 when the site emitters began logging their jal for SMC_REUSE
# (docs/PCARG-SIDE.md section 9: the lab translators grew 384 B).
LAYOUT_PAD_XLAT_BYTES=5504
